      "answer": "When a hand hygiene improvement programme has to be initiated from scratch, the essential steps are: Step 1, Facility preparedness – readiness for action; Step 2, Baseline evaluation – establishing the current situation; Step 3, Implementation – introducing the improvement activities; Step 4, Follow-up evaluation – evaluating the implementation impact; and Step 5, Action planning and review cycle – developing a plan for the next 5 years (minimum).",
